jdk.hotspot.agent: don't build libsaproc on android

ps_core.c reads prstatus_t out of a core file's NT_PRSTATUS notes. That type
comes from <sys/procfs.h>, which bionic does not ship, so the library cannot
compile at all:

  ps_core.c:190:4: error: use of undeclared identifier 'prstatus_t'

libsaproc is the native half of the Serviceability Agent (jhsdb, jmap -F and
friends) -- a post-mortem debugger, not something the JVM needs to run. Drop
it on android the way termux-packages does
(0005-android-prevent-build-of-libsa), but gate the change instead of removing
the target outright, so the linux/macos/windows builds here keep their SA.

The gate keys on OPENJDK_TARGET_OS plus OPENJDK_TARGET_LIBC: android is the
only linux target whose libc configure reports as neither gnu nor musl.

diff --git a/make/modules/jdk.hotspot.agent/Lib.gmk b/make/modules/jdk.hotspot.agent/Lib.gmk
index ed8de63..087fe98 100644
--- a/make/modules/jdk.hotspot.agent/Lib.gmk
+++ b/make/modules/jdk.hotspot.agent/Lib.gmk
@@ -80,6 +80,14 @@ $(eval $(call SetupJdkLibrary, BUILD_LIBSAPROC, \
     LIBS_windows := dbgeng.lib, \
 ))
 
-TARGETS += $(BUILD_LIBSAPROC)
+# libsaproc's core-file reader needs prstatus_t from <sys/procfs.h>, which
+# bionic does not ship. Android is the linux target whose libc configure
+# reports as neither gnu nor musl, so skip the library there and leave every
+# other target building it.
+SA_ON_BIONIC := $(if $(filter linux, $(OPENJDK_TARGET_OS)),$(if $(filter gnu musl, $(OPENJDK_TARGET_LIBC)),,true))
+
+ifneq ($(SA_ON_BIONIC), true)
+  TARGETS += $(BUILD_LIBSAPROC)
+endif
 
 ################################################################################
